.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt DUP 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm dup
.Nd duplicate a scheme-file handle with a rights mask
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x65).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call is part of the scheme IPC protocol (see
.Xr scheme 7
and
.Pa architecture/03-system-servers.md ).
.Pp
.Nm
creates a second kernel handle for the same open-file description.  The
server-side file id and the sequential cursor are shared; a
.Xr read 2
or
.Xr write 2
through either handle advances the one cursor.  The server increments the
description's reference count and releases it only at the last
.Xr close 2 .
.Pp
The rights mask reduces the rights of the new kernel handle.  It does not create
a new server file id and it does not reset the cursor.
.Pp
The kernel sends a reliable
.Dv Dup
notification before it returns; if the notification cannot be queued, the
duplicate is closed and the syscall fails.  The server increments the
open-file-description reference count.  The kernel's last close sends one CLOSE
per server reference, so the description is released only after every duplicate
and transferred reference is gone.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
A new SchemeFile handle on success.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er -offset indent
.It Er EBADF
The source handle is not a scheme-file handle.
.It Er EINVAL
The rights mask is invalid.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
